This work focuses on the existence and uniqueness of the positive solution to a class of high-order quasilinear elliptic equations with odd nonlinearity in N-dimensional space. These equations have the form $(-1)^{m-1}  \text{div}  \left(\vert x\vert^\alpha
A(x)\cdot\nabla u\vert|^{\frac{1}{\alpha}}\vert x\vert^{-\alpha}
\frac{x}{\vert\vert\vert}+\lambda\vert\vert^{m-1}u\right)$ in a domain $\Omega\subset R^N$, where $x\in\Omega$, $m\geq3$, $\alpha\in(0,\infty)$, $\lambda\in R$, $A(x)\in C^2(\Omega;R^N)$, and $A(x)\cdot\frac{x}{\vert\vert\vert}\neq0$ in $\Omega$. The results are applied to study the existence and uniqueness of the positive solution to a class of high-order quasilinear parabolic equations.
